       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <div class="blog-content">
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Joint Entrance Examination Main Session 2 Result 2026 – Scorecard Download Link">
             <div class="blog-body">
                <h1 class="blog-title">JEE Main Session 2 Result 2026: Your Gateway to Engineering Dreams!</h1>
                <p>The anticipation is building for lakhs of engineering aspirants as the National Testing Agency (NTA) prepares to announce the Joint Entrance Examination (JEE) Main Session 2 Result 2026. This critical examination paves the way for admissions to prestigious NITs, IIITs, GFTIs, and serves as the qualifying exam for JEE Advanced. With the Session 2 exams recently concluded, candidates are eagerly awaiting their scorecards, which hold the key to their future academic pursuits.</p>

                <p>Here’s a comprehensive guide to everything you need to know about downloading your JEE Main Session 2 Scorecard for 2026, understanding its details, and preparing for the subsequent counselling process.</p>

                <h2 class="section-title">Key Dates and Official Links</h2>
                <p>Stay informed with these crucial dates and official portals for your JEE Main Session 2 Result 2026.</p>
                <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                  <p>✅ **JEE Main Session 2 Exam Dates:** April 2 to April 9, 2026</p>
                  <p>✅ **Expected Result Date:** April 20, 2026 (NTA often releases results a day or two earlier)</p>
                  <p>✅ **Official Websites to Check Results:** jeemain.nta.nic.in and nta.ac.in</p>
                  <p>✅ **Scorecard Availability:** The scorecard will be available for download until July 31, 2026</p>
                </div>

                <h2 class="section-title">How to Download Your JEE Main Session 2 Scorecard 2026: A Step-by-Step Guide</h2>
                <p>Once the results are declared, accessing your scorecard is a straightforward process. Follow these detailed steps to download your JEE Main 2026 Session 2 Scorecard:</p>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official NTA JEE Main Website</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">Navigate to <a href="https://jeemain.nta.nic.in" target="_blank">jeemain.nta.nic.in</a>. This is the primary portal for all JEE Main related announcements and results. You can also check nta.ac.in.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the Result Link</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, look for a prominent link that says "JEE Main 2026 Session 2 Result" or "View Score Card JEE Main 2026". Click on this link.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">3. Enter Your Login Credentials</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">You will be redirected to a login page. Here, you need to enter your JEE Main Application Number and your Password or Date of Birth. Ensure you have these details ready to avoid any last-minute hassle.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">4. Input Security Pin/CAPTCHA</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">Some portals may require you to enter a security pin or complete a CAPTCHA verification to proceed. Carefully type the characters shown on the screen.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">5. Submit and View Result</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">After entering all the required details, click on the "Submit" button. Your JEE Main 2026 Session 2 Scorecard will be displayed on your screen.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">6. Download and Print</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">It is highly recommended to download the PDF version of your scorecard and take multiple printouts for future reference. This document is essential for the counselling process.</div>
                </div>

                <div class="highlight-text">
                  <p><strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Due to heavy traffic on result day, the website might be slow. If you face issues, wait a few minutes and try again. Do not rely on unofficial websites for your results.</p>
                </div>

                <h2 class="section-title">Understanding Your JEE Main 2026 Scorecard</h2>
                <p>Your JEE Main Session 2 Scorecard is more than just a piece of paper; it's a comprehensive report of your performance. Here's what you'll find on it:</p>
                <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                  <p>✅ **Application Number:** Your unique identification for the examination.</p>
                  <p>✅ **Candidate's Name, Guardian's Name, Category, Gender, Nationality:** Personal details as provided during registration.</p>
                  <p>✅ **Subject-wise NTA Scores (Percentile):** Your performance in Physics, Chemistry, and Mathematics, expressed in percentile.</p>
                  <p>✅ **Total NTA Score (Percentile):** Your overall percentile score, calculated using the normalization process across shifts and sessions.</p>
                  <p>✅ **All India Rank (AIR):** Your rank among all candidates who appeared for JEE Main 2026.</p>
                  <p>✅ **Category Rank:** If applicable, your rank within your specific reservation category.</p>
                  <p>✅ **Qualifying Status for JEE Advanced:** Indication of whether you are eligible to appear for JEE Advanced 2026.</p>
                </div>

                <h2 class="section-title">What's Next? Navigating JoSAA Counselling 2026</h2>
                <p>For qualified candidates, the next significant step is the Joint Seat Allocation Authority (JoSAA) counselling. This online process manages admissions to IITs, NITs, IIITs, and GFTIs. JoSAA counselling for JEE Main 2026 is expected to begin in June 2026, after the JEE Advanced results are declared.</p>

                <p>The counselling involves several stages:</p>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">1. Online Registration</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">Candidates must register on the official JoSAA portal using their JEE Main application number and password/security pin.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">2. Choice Filling and Locking</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">You will select your preferred colleges and courses from the available list. It's crucial to research thoroughly and prioritize your choices carefully.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">3. Seat Allotment</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">Seats are allotted based on your JEE Main/Advanced rank, category, and the choices you filled. JoSAA conducts multiple rounds of seat allotment.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">4. Seat Acceptance, Document Verification, and Fee Payment</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">If you are allotted a seat, you must accept it, pay the seat acceptance fee, and upload the required documents for online verification.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">5. Reporting to the Allotted Institute</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">Finally, you will need to report to your allotted institute for physical document verification and to confirm your admission.</div>
                </div>

                <h2 class="section-title">JEE Main 2026 Expected Cutoffs for JEE Advanced Qualification</h2>
                <p>The JEE Main cutoff for JEE Advanced qualification will be released by the NTA along with the Session 2 results. Based on expert analysis and past trends, here are the anticipated cutoff percentiles for various categories:</p>

                <table>
                  <thead>
                    <tr>
                      <th>Category</th>
                      <th>Expected JEE Main 2026 Qualifying Cutoff (Percentile)</th>
                      <th>Notes</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td>General (UR)</td>
                      <td>93.3 - 95.0</td>
                      <td>Expected to be highly competitive, possibly slightly increasing from previous years.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>General-EWS</td>
                      <td>80 - 82</td>
                      <td></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>OBC-NCL</td>
                      <td>79 - 82</td>
                      <td></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>SC</td>
                      <td>60 - 64</td>
                      <td></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>ST</td>
                      <td>47 - 51</td>
                      <td></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>PwD</td>
                      <td>~0.11</td>
                      <td></td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
                <p class="small text-muted"><em>These are projected figures based on past trends and are subject to change based on the total number of candidates and the difficulty level of the exam.</em></p>

                <h2 class="section-title">Essential Documents for JoSAA Counselling</h2>
                <p>Be prepared with these documents for a smooth counselling process:</p>
                <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                  <p>✅ Three passport-sized photographs (same as uploaded during JEE Main application)</p>
                  <p>✅ JEE Main Admit Card</p>
                  <p>✅ JEE Main Scorecard 2026</p>
                  <p>✅ Class 10th Marksheet (for Date of Birth proof)</p>
                  <p>✅ Class 12th Marksheet or equivalent</p>
                  <p>✅ Provisional Seat Allotment Letter (issued by JoSAA)</p>
                  <p>✅ Proof of Seat Acceptance Fee Payment</p>
                  <p>✅ Government-issued Photo Identification Card</p>
                  <p>✅ Category Certificate (if applicable)</p>
                  <p>✅ Medical Certificate (if applicable)</p>
                  <p>✅ Certificate for Persons with Disabilities (PWD) (if applicable)</p>
                </div>

                <h2 class="section-title">Final Thoughts</h2>
                <p>The JEE Main Session 2 Result 2026 marks a pivotal moment in your academic journey. While the wait can be nerve-wracking, remember to stay calm and follow the official instructions. Prepare your documents, understand the counselling process, and look forward to embarking on your engineering adventure. We wish all candidates the very best for their results!</p>
             </div>
             </div>
       </div>

            
            
